    "badge": "Best Value",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Low price per square foot",
      "Attached pad included",
      "Stocked in-store at Home Depot in many colors",
      "Easy to buy extra cartons for repairs",
      "Simple click joint for DIY installs"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Wear layer varies widely by collection, so read each label",
      "Thinner lines show subfloor flaws"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The easiest good-enough vinyl plank to buy and install for most rooms.",
    "description": "Lifeproof is Home Depot's house brand of rigid-core vinyl, and its biggest advantage is availability: you can see the planks in person, buy them the same day and come back for more cartons from the same shelf. Most collections include an attached pad, so there is no separate underlayment to buy for a wood subfloor, though you still need a vapor barrier on concrete. The catch is that Lifeproof is a brand umbrella, not one product, and wear layers range from thin builder grades to thicker lines. For a bedroom or rental, the entry lines are fine. For a kitchen or dog-heavy living room, choose a Lifeproof collection with a 12 to 20 mil wear layer and pay the small difference. Owners commonly report an easy install and a few cracked tongues when they forced the joints, so tap gently. Pricing is typically roughly $2 to $4 per square foot at the time of writing."
  },
  {
    "id": "shaw-floorte-pro",
    "name": "Shaw Floorté Pro",
    "category": "Stone Core, Light Commercial Lines",
    "badge": "Best for Heavy Traffic",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Rigid stone core resists dents from furniture and appliances",
      "Many collections carry 20 mil wear layers",
      "Light commercial warranties on several lines",
      "Large color and size range",
      "Stable in rooms with temperature swings"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Firm, can sound hard without a good pad",
